@flexiarg task-selection/end-in-something-shown
@title End In Something Shown
@keywords demonstration, verifiable capability, dispatch, demo, artefact
@audience agents dispatching work; War Machine outer loop
@tone design
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-10-28 (claude-11, witnesses K12)
@role gate
@guard needs: for each candidate, the capability it would demonstrate and how someone could verify it.
@effect removes candidates that cannot end in a verifiable demonstrated capability, or reshapes them until they can.
@predicts each dispatch ends with something a person can check working.
@references [task-selection/halfway-house task-selection/the-date-decides]
! conclusion: Select only work that ends in a capability someone can verify, and shrink work that cannot until it does.

  + context: Agents can run long and report activity; the operator needs to see things work.

  + IF:
    A candidate's end state is "progress" rather than something shown.

  + HOWEVER:
    Long all-out runs look productive and some real work has no visible end for a long time; an end-to-end demonstration chosen too early fails and has to be cut back.

  + THEN:
    Require each dispatch to name what it will demonstrate and how it is checked. If a full demonstration is premature, select the smaller demonstrable step (harness plus tests) and drop the larger claim from the packet.

  + BECAUSE:
    Work that ends in nothing shown cannot be told apart from work that did nothing.

  + evidence:
    - memory every-dispatch-demonstrates-a-feature (Joe 2026-09-30): "Every dispatch ... must end in a demonstrated feature someone can verify ... Long all-out runs that end with no demonstrated capability are ruled out."
    - futon3c/holes/missions/M-apm-demonstration.md:5833-5839 (Joe 2026-08-14): "frame-1 is the demo, let's build it", then cut to "harness + stage tests + refusal tests; no end-to-end claim".
    - futon3c/holes/missions/M-war-machine-pilot.md:26-31 (Joe 2026-05-24): "I would like to put this to the test."
    - futon7/holes/M-demonstration-foundry.md:15-19: demonstrations of value-add needed on a cadence.
